Allocate root values from per-thread cells in uncollectable slabs.

`allocRootValue` allocated each root's `shared_ptr` control block with
`traceable_allocator`: `GC_MALLOC_UNCOLLECTABLE` to make it and
`GC_FREE` to free it, each under the collector's global lock. huggorm
roots every Python `Value`, so threads walking one state's values took
that lock twice per value (nixidae/nixidae#1557).

The block now lives in a 32-byte cell carved from a 4096-cell slab that
the collector always scans. Each thread keeps up to 128 free cells and
moves 64 at a time to or from a shared list, which a mutex guards. A
thread's cells go back to the shared list when it exits. `RootValue`
keeps its type, so no caller changes. Determinate Nix has the same
slabs in `root-value.cc`; nix-determinate-thread-local-root-slots adds
the per-thread cache there.

